- Native linker: some features missing, falling back to external linker

- interchange and extended float types (just aliased, no __STDC_IEC_60559_TYPES__)

- add more cheap -O1 passes, without SSA analysis.
  Ranked candidates, all doable without SSA:
  1. Switch lowering — today every switch case is a linear cmp+jcc chain (codegen.c:13083). Already in TODO:
     dense small ints → jump table (the &&label label-address machinery this needs already exists),
     sparse → sorted binary search. sparse small ints (elsif chains), sparse large ints (perfect hashes).
     Biggest single win; no dataflow.
  2. x86 peephole parity — asm_peep_try() is #ifdef ARCH_ARM64 only. The mov+mov fold,
     mov-imm+ALU→ALU-imm fold, and identity-op deletion all have direct x86 equivalents. Mechanical port
     of existing logic.
  3. Algebraic identities in optimize_node — codegen only sees const-on-RHS (x+0, x*1 at
     codegen.c:16515). 0+x, 1*x, x<<0, x/1, x%1, !!x, and const-on-left normalization are trivial AST
     walker additions. (Guard x*0→0 on side-effect-free lhs.)
  4. Block-local copy/const propagation — one forward pass per straight-line block: a=5; b=a+1 → b=6,
     store-to-load forwarding. No SSA: small map keyed by LVar->offset (the CTFE env in opt.c already
     uses offset/8 as its key), invalidated by any call, pointer store, or address-taken local.
  5. Block-local dead-store elimination — same pass as #4: x=1; x=2; drops the first store if not volatile;
     unused-result x++ drops the inc. Requires the local-not-address-taken check, same invalidation set.
  6. Jump threading — jcc .L1 … .L1: jmp .L2 → retarget .L1 users to .L2; jmp to the
     immediately-following label → delete. Pure fixup-table surgery on the emitted buffer, no analysis.
  7. Unused pure-call statements — strlen(x); as an expression statement → drop. fn_purity() and the
     pure-fn table already exist in opt.c:78; this is just a statement-list filter.

- -O2 Tail calls — return f(args) → jmp f. Non-SSA but ABI-sensitive (frame layout, varargs callee)

- SSA conversion for -O2, and the usual optimizations with SSA, as in xcc, antcc or ccc.

- optional solver backend for the optimizer and contracts prover with -O3
